53mid\u001b[39m (e.g. \u001b[38;5;153macme\u001b[39m). - Without it, unchanged. - Unknown id\r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m\u001b[3m→ error naming the id. Where to implement filtering? Could do in cli.ts, filtering \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m     \u001b[2m\u001b[3minvoice array before passing to summarize/aging. But then testing? Best to add a \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m\u001b[3mfunction perhaps in invoice.ts or parse.ts? Let's think about design cleanly. \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m\u001b[3mOptions: 1. In cli.ts: parse \u001b[38;5;153m--customer\u001b[39m from rest args, filter invoices. Error if \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bnone match. 2. Add a filtering helper e.g. \u001b[38;5;153msrc/filter.ts\u001b[39m with \u001b[38;5;153mforCustomer(invoices, \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bid)\u001b[39m that throws InvoiceFileError? Hmm, it's not really a file error — the id isn't in\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bthe file. But cli catches InvoiceFileError only and prints \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer: msg\u001b[39m, exit 1. A \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bseparate error class could be used but must be caught. Th…\r\u001b[36C\u001b[2B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246mthought for 19s)\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
